-- title:
--   Unique lifting mod π from square-zero thickenings
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$, and let $f_M : M \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $C$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and write $M_C$ for the base change of $f_M$ along $\operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, realised as the second projection of the pullback; for a $C$-algebra $S$, an $S$-point of $M_C$ means a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} S \to M_C$ whose composite with that projection is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $C \to S$. Let $PR$ be an `AlgFunctor` over $C$, that is, an assignment of a type $PR(S)$ to each commutative $C$-algebra $S$ together with maps $PR(\varphi) : PR(S) \to PR(S')$ for $C$-algebra homomorphisms $\varphi$, compatible with identities and composition, and let $\tau_S : PR(S) \to M_C(S)$ be a family of structure maps. Assume two hypotheses. First, naturality: for every $C$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : S \to S'$ and every $x \in PR(S)$, the underlying morphism of $\tau_{S'}(PR(\varphi)(x))$ is $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by that of $\tau_S(x)$. Second, an infinitesimal lifting property: for every surjection $p : S \to S_0$ of $C$-algebras with $S$ Noetherian and $(\ker p)^2 = 0$, every $x_0 \in PR(S_0)$ and every $S$-point $t$ of $M_C$ whose composite with $\operatorname{Spec} p$ is the morphism underlying $\tau_{S_0}(x_0)$, there is a unique $x \in PR(S)$ with $PR(p)(x) = x_0$ and $\tau_S(x) = t$. The conclusion is the same lifting statement for reduction modulo $\pi$: for every Noetherian $C$-algebra $T$, writing $\bar T = T/(\pi)$ for the quotient by the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $T$, every $\bar x \in PR(\bar T)$ and every $T$-point $t$ of $M_C$ whose composite with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map is the morphism underlying $\tau_{\bar T}(\bar x)$, there is a unique $x \in PR(T)$ with $PR(T \to \bar T)(x) = \bar x$ and $\tau_T(x) = t$.
--
--   This is the point-functor form of the passage from unique lifting along square-zero thickenings to unique lifting along the nilpotent thickening $T \to T/\pi T$, as in the formally étale lifting criteria of EGA IV §17.1. It is used in the construction of the algebraic point functor representing the rigidified-curve strata in the Čerednik–Drinfeld fine moduli argument, where it supplies the reduction-modulo-$\pi$ clause from the square-zero one.
